Compose examples for the boat computer
======================================

Installed read-only at /usr/share/boat/compose-examples/. Nothing in here runs
by itself: these are reference stacks to copy and edit, not a deployment.

How the pieces fit
------------------
  boat-compose.service   runs /usr/bin/boat-compose-up at boot
  boat-compose-up        brings up /data/compose/docker-compose.yml, if one
                         has been seeded there, and does nothing otherwise
  /data/compose          YOUR stack - hand-managed config-as-code, meant to be
                         kept under git so an update is a pull and a restart

To deploy one of these:

    mkdir -p /data/compose
    cp /usr/share/boat/compose-examples/signalk.yml.example \
       /data/compose/docker-compose.yml
    $EDITOR /data/compose/docker-compose.yml     # read the header first
    systemctl start boat-compose

The CLI is the v2 plugin: `docker compose` (a space), not the hyphenated v1
`docker-compose`. The v1 client that this project's kirkstone-era
meta-virtualization packages is broken on this image; boat-docker-compose-plugin
vendors the official static v2 binary and that is what boat-compose-up runs.

The files
---------
  signalk.yml.example      Signal K server. READ ITS HEADER: it runs
                           privileged and mounts the docker socket, which is
                           root-equivalent control of the host.
  browser.yml.example      a browser in a container on the HDMI screen, with
                           the X cookie mounted from /run/boat-x11
  firefox.yml.example      linuxserver/firefox - brings its own KasmVNC
                           desktop on :3000, reached from a browser on any
                           other machine. It never touches the host display,
                           so it needs none of the X wiring above - and it is
                           the wrong answer if what you want is a window on
                           the Jetson's own screen.
  x11-app.yml.example      the smallest thing that proves the X path works
  deepstream.yml.example   NVIDIA DeepStream, GPU + camera
  Dockerfile.firefox.example  what browser.yml.example builds from

Every one of them mounts host resources. Read the header of each file before
running it: they document what is being handed to the container and why, and
several of those grants are wide.
